+ *     "debug_messages" in "presenter".
+ *   d3d11_force_caps=key=0[,key=0..]  TEST: masks probed capabilities so that the fallbacks of a GPU without them can
+ *     be exercised on any GPU. Keys: nv12_srv, p010_srv (the decoder pool cannot have SHADER_RESOURCE; decoder_srv=0
+ *     means both), p010 (the video processor takes no P010 input), rotate, mirror, procamp, shader (no pixel shader
+ *     route), cuda_import (the presenter cannot import CUDA frames). The mask applies to the presenter of the open and to
+ *     ffp_probe_caps_opts, where masked capabilities read as false and the d3d11 entry gets "forced":["p010=0",..].
+ *     Every masked key is listed as "force_caps:<key>=0" in the presenter's "fallbacks".
+ *   d3d11_route=vp|shader  forces the d3d11 presenter route (VideoProcessor / pixel shader). A frame that cannot take
+ *     it uses the normal choice ("route_forced_unavailable:<route>" in the fallbacks); "route_forced:<route>" otherwise.
+ *     CUDA frames always take the CUDA shader route; the option does not apply to them.
+ * ffp_get_debug_info "presenter" (d3d11 in use) gets "adapter":{"name":"..","vendor_id":N,"luid":"HHHHHHHH:LLLLLLLL"}
+ * (the GPU of the presenter), "debug_layer":bool, "debug_messages":N and "fallbacks":[".."]: the distinct short names of
+ * the fallbacks the presenter took, in order of first occurrence ("decoder_pool_no_srv", "p010_vp_unsupported:shader",
+ * "p010_vp_unsupported:download", "format_download:<pix_fmt>", "foreign_device_download" (a D3D11 frame of another device),
+ * "route_forced:<vp|shader>", "route_forced_unavailable:<vp|shader>", "force_caps:<key>=0"). */
+
