+ * the SDL renderer: system-memory frames, SDL textures) | "d3d11" (see below). Frames that the presenter cannot take
+ * are converted / downloaded. If a presenter cannot be set up, or fails later (device lost, Present / Blt
+ * errors), FFP_EVENT_PRESENTER_ERROR (9) is raised with {"presenter":"d3d11","error":"...","fallback":"sdl"} and the
+ * player continues with the SDL presenter for the rest of this open (hardware frames are downloaded from then on).
+ * When the failure is a lost GPU device (DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED / DEVICE_RESET / DEVICE_HUNG /
+ * DRIVER_INTERNAL_ERROR, or ID3D11Device::GetDeviceRemovedReason() != S_OK at the failure) the event also has
+ * "device_lost":true,"removed_reason":"0x887a0005" (the HRESULT): the host should open again on a new device instead
+ * of treating d3d11 as unusable. A decoder error of an open whose d3d11 device was removed carries the same two members
+ * in its FFP_EVENT_ERROR json. The removed device is released when the media is closed (ffp_stop / ffp_open); nothing
+ * of it (device, video processor, views) survives into the next open, which creates a new device on the
+ * d3d11_adapter_luid it was given.
+ * ffp_get_debug_info has a "presenter" object: {"name":"sdl"|"d3d11" (in use),"requested":..,"params":{..},"error":"",
+ * "frames_direct":N,"frames_uploaded":M}.
+ *
+ * ffp_set_presenter_params(json) / open option presenter_params=<json>: parameters that the presenter applies when it
+ * draws, instead of filters in the video graph:
+ *   {"rotation":90,"flip_h":false,"flip_v":false,"eq":{"brightness":0.1,"contrast":1.2,"saturation":1,"gamma":1}}
+ * rotation is clockwise (0, 90, 180, 270), the flips are applied after the rotation (the same result as the filters
+ * transpose, then hflip / vflip), eq has the ffmpeg eq filter semantics (brightness -1..1, contrast, saturation 0..3,
+ * gamma). The object replaces all parameters: absent members are identity, "eq":null switches eq off. The parameters
+ * are used from the next displayed frame (the current picture is redrawn when paused), persist across ffp_open and
+ * ffp_stop until changed, and also shape ffp_snapshot (the rotated size, rotation / flip / eq applied).
+ * Returns FFP_EINVAL, without changing anything, for bad JSON or for a value the presenter in effect cannot apply. With
+ * the SDL presenter only identity parameters are accepted (the host keeps rotation / flip / eq in the filter graph).
+ * "In effect" is the presenter of the last ffp_open (SDL before the first one, and after a fallback to SDL). */
+FFP_API int         FFP_CALL ffp_set_presenter_params(FFPlayer *p, const char *json);
+
+/* presenter=d3d11 (hosted window only: ffp_create with an HWND): a flip-model DXGI swap chain on a child window that
+ * fills the host window's client area and follows its size (it never touches the host window itself, the SDL renderer
+ * stays untouched underneath and takes over after a fallback; no top-level window is created or shown). Every
+ * picture is drawn with ID3D11VideoProcessor::VideoProcessorBlt (colour space from the frame: BT.601 / 709 / 2020,
+ * limited / full; the source rectangle is the frame's crop; the destination rectangle is the aspect-correct
+ * letterbox with the SAR; vsync). The decoder shares the presenter's ID3D11Device: with hwaccel=d3d11va (or auto
+ * choosing d3d11va) an AVHWDeviceContext wrapping that device is the decoder device, and D3D11 NV12 / P010 frames are
+ * shown without any copy. With presenter=d3d11 and a D3D11VA device hwframes defaults to "keep" (hwframes=download
+ * still forces a download at decode time): the frames reach the presenter even when vf is empty (extending the rule of
+ * hwframes=keep: a frame the presenter shows as is is not downloaded after the filter graph either). Frames of other
+ * hardware domains (cuda, ...) are downloaded after the graph. System frames are uploaded once (NV12 / P010
+ * through a D3D11 surface pool, swscale to NV12 / P010 / BGRA for other formats). Subtitles are not drawn by this
+ * presenter (use sn or burn them with a filter). The audio visualisation of audio-only media is drawn by SDL.
+ * Rotation uses VideoProcessorSetStreamRotation, mirroring VideoProcessorSetStreamMirror (ID3D11VideoContext1) when the
+ * driver really mirrors (verified by a self test at the first use; otherwise ffp_set_presenter_params with flips
+ * returns FFP_EINVAL), eq uses the video processor's brightness / contrast / saturation filters (the honoured ranges
+ * are in the "presenters" entry of ffp_probe_caps); gamma is not supported (!= 1 returns FFP_EINVAL).
+ * ffp_snapshot renders the retained frame through the video processor into an offscreen BGRA texture of the size
+ * documented for ffp_snapshot after the rotation (90 / 270 swap width and height before the SAR stretch), with the
+ * rotation / flip / eq of the presenter parameters applied.
+ * open option presenter_debug_fail = "display" (also "1") | "init" | "device_lost": TEST ONLY, makes the presenter fail
