+/**
+ * @file
+ * libffplay D3D11 presenter: a flip-model DXGI swap chain on a child window of the host window, every frame
+ * is shown with ID3D11VideoProcessor::VideoProcessorBlt (colour conversion, scaling, rotation, mirroring and
+ * procamp in the driver's video engine). The decoder shares the presenter's ID3D11Device (an AVHWDeviceContext
+ * wraps it), so decoded D3D11 frames are shown without any copy. System frames are uploaded once.
+ *
+ * eq mapping (ffmpeg eq filter semantics -> D3D11 video processor filter levels; the driver ranges come from
+ * GetVideoProcessorFilterRange, the behaviour of the brightness filter is measured by ffp_calibrate_procamp()):
+ *   saturation: level = s * Default (the neutral level; 100 on NVIDIA, range 13..187 = ffmpeg 0.13..1.87)
+ *   contrast:   level = c * Default (NVIDIA 40..160 = 0.4..1.6). The video processor scales about black, eq about mid
+ *               grey (luma code 128 = RGB 130.4), so  eq(x) = c * x + 130.4 * (1 - c)  and the offset goes to brightness
+ *   brightness: eq adds b * 255 to the luma code = b * 297 RGB codes (255 * 255 / 219, limited -> full range); the driver's
+ *               brightness filter moves RGB by bri_k codes per level (measured with a flat NV12 gray: 1.0 on NVIDIA, range
+ *               -101..101) and acts after the contrast scaling (measured; before it: the level is divided by c):
+ *               level = (b * 297 + 130.4 * (1 - c)) / bri_k, which gives the honoured brightness range [-0.34, 0.34] at
+ *               contrast 1 (a contrast other than 1 uses part of it)
+ *   gamma has no video processor equivalent: != 1 is rejected.
